==Etymology==
Alien X's name is made up of "[[Wikipedia:Alien|alien]]", a reference to him being an extraterrestrial life form, as well as a transformation, and "X", the roman numeral for 10, which refers to both his mysteriousness and the fact that he is [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s tenth alien in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''. "X" is also used as an unknown variable, which references how Alien X's appearance and powers were kept secret until his debut.

==Trivia==
*[[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]], [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]], and [[Professor Paradox]] all acknowledge that Alien X is the most powerful being in the [[Omnitrix]].<ref name="TFoC" />
**However, Ben has conceded that transforming into Alien X is not worth the cost, as the risk is simply too great for him to use the transformation.<ref name="X=B+2" />{{Refn|[[:File:Magazine Alien X Data.png]]|group = mag}} Simply put, Alien X is too much of a pain for Ben to use unless there is no other option.{{Refn|http://archive.is/RUkwK|group = DJW}}
**Originally, Alien X was not the most powerful alien in the Omnitrix.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien X Not the Most Powerful Alien.PNG]]|group = DM}} This is retconned in ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', where it is revealed that [[Celestialsapien (Classic)|Celestialsapien]]s possess the greatest power in the [[Universe (Classic)|universe]].{{Refn|group = BTP|name = retcons}}
*Sometime between the events of ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'' and ''The Forge of Creation'', Ben had had the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] modified to lock Alien X, to both prevent himself from accidentally transforming into him and as a safety measure to keep someone like [[Albedo]] from using it. The only way to access Alien X was to use a pair of [[Ultimatrix Security Keys|keys]] in [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]]'s possession. This is not the case for the new [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]], in which Alien X is accessible without any keys, as the threat of Albedo turning into Alien X has been neutralized because Albedo can transform into aliens that Ben had unlocked in the Ultimatrix prior to ''[[Double or Nothing]]'',{{Refn|[[:File:Albedo Cannot Add More Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Feedback's DNA Not in Alteration Field.PNG]]|group = DJW}} which did not include Alien X.
*In ''[[Andreas' Fault]]'', a fan of Ben referred to the Alien X smoothie as a disappointment as well as saying it tastes like "filler". This is a reference to the fan reactions to Alien X at the time.
*In ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', [[Rook Blonko|Rook]] spoke of Alien X, but believed he was just a rumor. Ben tried to convince him that Alien X is real, but Rook didn't believe him and asked Ben to transform and show him, which Ben refused.
**This conversation happened again in ''[[So Long, and Thanks for All the Smoothies]]'', and by the end of the episode, Rook saw Alien X in person.
*In ''[[Universe vs. Tennyson]]'', Ben offered to let the two personalities argue between themselves for eternity if they gave him full control over Alien X. [[Serena]] agrees, followed by an initially reluctant [[Bellicus]], giving Ben full control over Alien X. This was seen again in ''[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]''.
*In many promotional images and the openings to '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Alien X is posing dramatically. This is ironic, considering that he is frozen in an upright position for most of the time in the series proper.
*Alien X was the first alien introduced in '''Alien Force''' and '''Ultimate Alien''' to not be voiced by [[Dee Bradley Baker]]; the second being [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]].
*During the first half of Season 1 of '''Alien Force''', the opening of the show only displayed a silhouette of Alien X because he was meant to be a surprise alien. However, part of his face could be seen on the bottom right of the screen. After ''[[X = Ben + 2]]'', the intro began showing Alien X's full image.
*Alien X's starred body is not simply "aesthetic". Like all Celestialsapiens, Alien X contains his own "debate dimension", which exists inside his head.{{Refn|[[:File:Milleous and Attea Royalty.PNG]]|group = DM}}
**This explains how Paradox was able to travel inside Alien X and speak to Ben whilst he was arguing with Bellicus and Serena before reversing the transformation.<ref name="TFoC" />{{Refn|[[:File:UA S1 Young Ben.PNG]]|group = DM}}
**However, [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] believed that it is actually a visual interpretation of what is happening mentally.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien X Debate Dimension.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Much like his birthplace, Alien X exists outside the universe (i.e. time and space). Beings existing outside time and space are simultaneously everywhere and nowhere at the same time.{{Refn|group=DR|name=tweet1|[[:File:Alien X Exist Outside Space and Time.png]]}}
**This also implies that since Ben Prime and [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] share the same Celestialsapien DNA in their Omnitrices, the Alien X transformation used by them is the same Alien X, not just genetically, but literally.{{Refn|group=DR|name=tweet1}}
*Albedo's Bellicus and Serena would appear red.{{Refn|[[:File:Negative Serena and Bellicus.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Alien X had concept art drawn by [[Eric Canete]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eric Canete Designed Alien X and Chromastone Concepts.png]]|group = EC}} whereas his final design was created by [[Glenn Wong]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|https://archive.is/aZD1R|group = GW}}
*The original plan for Alien X had him with two faces talking to represent two personalities in one body. However, because of animation challenges and the fact that Alien X has one male and one female personality, which was not reflected by the faces, the idea was scrapped.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien X Original Plan.png]]|group = GM}}
*Various early production and promotional materials state that Alien X accidentally destroys a mountain range during his debut, indicating that plans changed.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/23/Hero_Generation_Series_Bible.pdf Hero Generation Series Bible]|group = HG Bible|name = bible}}{{Refn|group = Bandai|name = card}}
*When asked if he wished he could change one of his '''Omniverse''' designs, Derrick stated that he would probably give Alien X clothes.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick wished he gave Alien X clothes.png]]|group = DJW}} His clothes would look similar to those of [[Wikipedia:Parasite (comics)|Parasite]] from '''[[Wikipedia:Superman: The Animated Series|Superman: The Animated Series]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien X clothes would look like DCAU Parasite.png]]|group = DJW}}

